    {'heading': 'Lesson XXIV'},
    {'para': '**263. Declension. Stems in ⟨ant⟩ (or ⟨at⟩), cont’d. B. Stems in ⟨mant⟩ (⟨mat⟩) and ⟨vant⟩ (⟨vat⟩).** Adjectives formed with these suffixes are possessives. They are declined precisely alike∗; and differ in inflection from the participles in ⟨ant⟩ only by lengthening the ⟨a⟩ in the nom. sing. masc. The feminine is made in ⟨ī⟩; thus, ⟨śrīmatī⟩. In the dual neut. ⟨n⟩ is never inserted. Thus, ⟨śrīmant⟩, ‘rich’, ‘celebrated:’'},
